/-!
# All-root Weyl elements and the Borel–Weyl intersection

For a Chevalley datum `D`, `D.weylSubgroup A` is defined as the subgroup generated by the actual
torus `T_D(A)` and the pinned simple Weyl elements `n_{αᵢ}(1)`. Over every commutative ring `A`,
conjugation by `n_{αᵢ}(1)` sends `n_γ(s)` to `n_{sᵢ γ}(η_{αᵢ,γ} s)`. Since every root is in the
simple-reflection orbit of a simple root and `n_{αᵢ}(s) = h_{αᵢ}(s) n_{αᵢ}(1)`, every all-root
Weyl element `n_γ(s)` (`s : Aˣ`) already lies in `D.weylSubgroup A`, and `D.weylSubgroup A` is
equally generated by `T_D(A)` together with all `n_γ(1)`. Over a field `K`, `D.weylProjection K`
maps `n_γ(s)` to the reflection `s_γ` in `γ`.

The second part of this file proves the intersection identity `B(K) ∩ N(K) = T(K)` over every
field `K` (`borelSubgroup_inf_weylSubgroup_eq_range_torusPoints`), without assuming `K` is
infinite or algebraically closed:

1. Any `g ∈ B(K) ∩ N(K)` projects to `1` in the Weyl group, since a nontrivial Weyl element has a
   positive inversion `γ` and `g` would conjugate the nontrivial element `x_γ(1) ∈ B(K)` into a
   negative root subgroup, which meets `B(K)` trivially.
2. Factoring `g = u * t` (`u ∈ U(K)`, `t ∈ T(K)`) reduces to `U(K) ∩ N(K) = 1`. After base change
   to `AlgebraicClosure K`, trivial Weyl projection forces the matrix of `u` to commute with the
   represented full-weight diagonal torus, vanishing between distinct weight spaces; meanwhile
   ordering each weight space in the two opposite tie-breaking orders places `U` in the
   upper-unitriangular group for both orders, forcing `1` on the diagonal and `0` between distinct
   basis vectors of equal weight.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.weylElement_conj_weylElement`: `n_{αᵢ}(1)` conjugates
  `n_γ(s)` to `n_{sᵢ γ}(η_{αᵢ,γ} s)`.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.weylElement_unit_mem_weylSubgroup`: every `n_γ(s)` (`s : Aˣ`)
  lies in `D.weylSubgroup A`.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.weylSubgroup_eq_closure_allRoots`: `D.weylSubgroup A` is
  generated by `T_D(A)` and all `n_γ(1)`.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.weylProjection_weylElement_unit`: `D.weylProjection K` maps
  `n_γ(s)` to `s_γ`.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.positivePoints_inf_weylSubgroup_eq_bot`: `U(K) ∩ N(K) = 1`.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.ChevalleyDatum.borelSubgroup_inf_weylSubgroup_eq_range_torusPoints`:
  `B(K) ∩ N(K) = T(K)`.

## References

* R. Steinberg, *Lectures on Chevalley Groups*, Chapter 3, Lemmas 19–22 and Theorem 4.
* R. W. Carter, *Simple Groups of Lie Type*, §§7.2 and 8.2.
-/

public section

open Multiplicative TensorProduct TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra

